# xftest3.input — the callback example.
#
# "Hello world" carries a callback that prints "Hello world" and must NOT end the
# program (fl_do_forms only returns for the button without a callback); "Quit"
# ends the current fl_do_forms() call.  Geometry as in xftest2.input: the form is
# 230x180, "Hello world" is at (20,20) 190x60 and "Quit" at (70,100) 90x60.
#
# The example on xforms-toolkit.org calls fl_do_forms() twice in a row, so
# "Quit" has to be pressed once per call: the first press returns from the first
# fl_do_forms(), the second press from the second one, and only then does main()
# return.

motion 115 50
sleep 300
button press left
sleep 150
button release left
sleep 400

motion 115 130
sleep 200
button press left
sleep 150
button release left
sleep 500
button press left
sleep 150
button release left
sleep 800